# Build output.
#
# These patterns are anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored
# "manhattan" matches the cmd/manhattan DIRECTORY as well as the binary, which
# silently excluded the entire command-line interface from version control:
# `git add -A` skipped it without a word, and a fresh clone had no CLI at all.
# Anchor anything that shares a name with a directory.
/bin/
/dist/
/manhattan
/manhattan.exe

# Generated artifacts. Every one is reproducible with `./run.sh bench`, and
# checking them in would let a stale number outlive the run that made it.
/out/
/RESULTS.md

# The dashboard's build output IS committed, under cmd/manhattan/dist, because
# it is embedded into the Go binary. That keeps `go build ./...` working on a
# clean clone with no Node toolchain, which is what someone evaluating this
# with four minutes actually needs. Rebuild it with `./run.sh web`.
/web/node_modules/

# Local secrets.
.env
.env.local

# Tooling.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.prof
*.test
__pycache__/
.venv/
